{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-123645",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's call ${O}_{1}$ the event \"the first outcome is orange\", ${R}_{2}$ the event \"the second outcome is red\" and ${O}_{3}$ the event \"the third outcome is orange\". Then the required probability is $P({O}_{1}\\cap {R}_{2}\\cap {O}_{3}).$\n\nSince the events ${O}_{1}$, ${R}_{2}$ and ${O}_{3}$ are mutually independent, we can use the multiplication law for independent events, which states that\n\n$$\nP({O}_{1}\\cap {R}_{2}\\cap {O}_{3})=P({O}_{1})\\cdot P({R}_{2})\\cdot P({O}_{3}).\n$$\n\nLet's find $P({O}_{1}),P({R}_{2})$ and $P({O}_{3}).$\n\n- The spinner has $1$ orange section among the $1+6=7$ sections. So, we have\n\n$$\nP({O}_{1})=P({O}_{3})=\\frac{1}{7},\\,P({R}_{2})=\\frac{6}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting the above into the multiplication law for independent events, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({O}_{1}\\cap {R}_{2}\\cap {O}_{3}) & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{6}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{343}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
